codex
The full-covariance Gaussian approximation is far too biased in synthetic tests, even as a small blend. I’m keeping the estimator sample-based and will look for variance reductions that do not impose a Gaussian final-layer assumption.
codex
I’ll also test blending the current estimator with a radial-control/spherical estimator locally. The spherical estimate alone was worse, but if its error is partly independent it may still reduce variance at a small weight.
